{"ts": "2026-11-23T06:33:06.202179Z", "run_id": "r-20261123T0509Z-33fe", "unit": "openspec:add-mcp-client", "seq": 80, "type": "delegate.result", "question": "Q-002", "id": "Q-002", "status": "answered", "reason": "Checked in the repository: 0470_tool_registry.sql forces RLS on tool_server with a policy on app.tenant_id; roles.ts creates both roles NOBYPASSRLS and migrate.ts refuses a privileged owner, so option 2 is not viable; withTenantTx takes any pool with connect and the repo's other db tests (credentials/schema.test.ts and others) seed tool_server through withTenantTx(db.ownerPool, ...). The frozen test's seedToolServer and countRows use bare pool.query, so the implementer's diagnosis is correct and the clarifier suggestion matches the established pattern.", "called": true, "tasks": ["3.1"], "target": null, "kind": "technical", "profile": "delegate-fable", "model": "claude-fable-5-1", "cli": "claude-code", "cost_usd": 1.3251525, "decision": "accept", "answer_sha256": "8edc5d110e674fcb4fab4ef8b5fee4c241e7ff11f199fb8368e85e85e0b0505a", "checked": [{"ref": "src/tools/mcp/register.db.test.ts:23", "quote": "await pool.query(\n    `INSERT INTO ursitoare.tool_server", "claim": "seedToolServer inserts into tool_server with a bare pool query and no tenant setting."}, {"ref": "src/tools/mcp/register.db.test.ts:59", "quote": "const r = await pool.query<{ n: number }>(`SELECT count(*)::int AS n FROM ursitoare.${table}`);", "claim": "countRows selects without a tenant context, so forced RLS hides every row."}, {"ref": "src/tools/mcp/register.db.test.ts:101", "quote": "await seedToolServer(db.ownerPool, a.tenantId, \"srv_a\");", "claim": "The callers pass the owner pool, which is subject to RLS."}, {"ref": "src/db/migrations/0470_tool_registry.sql:13", "quote": "ALTER TABLE ursitoare.tool_server ENABLE ROW LEVEL SECURITY, FORCE ROW LEVEL SECURITY;", "claim": "tool_server forces RLS even for the table owner."}, {"ref": "src/db/migrations/0470_tool_registry.sql:15", "quote": "USING (tenant_id = current_setting('app.tenant_id', true))", "claim": "The policy depends on the app.tenant_id setting that withTenantTx sets."}, {"ref": "src/db/roles.ts:12", "quote": "const ROLE_ATTRIBUTES = \"LOGIN NOSUPERUSER NOCREATEDB NOCREATEROLE NOREPLICATION NOBYPASSRLS\";", "claim": "The owner role is created without BYPASSRLS."}, {"ref": "src/db/migrate.ts:152", "quote": "if (owner.rolsuper || owner.rolbypassrls) {\n    roleInvalid(\"owner_role_privileged\");", "claim": "Migrations refuse an owner that bypasses RLS, so option 2 is not viable."}, {"ref": "src/credentials/schema.test.ts:32", "quote": "await withTenantTx(db.ownerPool, { tenantId, reviewProfile: \"solo\" }, async (tx) => {", "claim": "Existing tests seed tool_server through the owner pool inside withTenantTx with exactly the suggested context."}, {"ref": "src/tenancy/tx.ts:6", "quote": "export type TenantPool = Pick<pg.Pool, \"connect\">;", "claim": "withTenantTx accepts the pg.Pool the test helpers already receive."}, {"ref": "spec:specs/tool-mcp/spec.md#requirement-registration-stores-the-endpoint-once-and-refuses-what-the-gateway-would", "quote": "forced row level security, `SELECT` and `INSERT` only for the application role", "claim": "mcp_server is also forced-RLS, so countRows must run under a tenant context."}]}
