{"ts": "2026-11-23T06:33:50.001472Z", "run_id": "r-20261123T0509Z-33fe", "unit": "openspec:add-mcp-client", "seq": 85, "type": "delegate.result", "question": "Q-003", "id": "Q-003", "status": "answered", "reason": "Read src/tools/mcp/register.db.test.ts: lines 134 to 144 loop over eleven bad endpoints and call seedToolServer(db.ownerPool, a.tenantId, \"srv_bad_check\") each time; seedToolServer (lines 18 to 30) is a plain INSERT into ursitoare.tool_server with no ON CONFLICT and runs outside attempt. The only cleanup is the DELETE FROM mcp_server at line 137. src/db/migrations/0470_tool_registry.sql line 12 declares PRIMARY KEY (tenant_id, tool_server_id) on tool_server, so the second seed of the same id violates it. This is a purely technical defect in a frozen red test; the clarifier suggestion names the file and gives a correct fix, so accept opens it for the next green.", "called": true, "tasks": ["3.1"], "target": null, "kind": "technical", "profile": "delegate-fable", "model": "claude-fable-5-1", "cli": "claude-code", "cost_usd": 0.831932, "decision": "accept", "answer_sha256": "322cac4df719f6f24939da3c674fe06403e23084724e961afef92e1ee492ba26", "checked": [{"ref": "src/tools/mcp/register.db.test.ts:134", "quote": "for (const endpoint of bad) {\n      await seedToolServer(db.ownerPool, a.tenantId, \"srv_bad_check\");", "claim": "Every iteration of the bad-endpoint loop seeds the same tool_server id srv_bad_check."}, {"ref": "src/tools/mcp/register.db.test.ts:23", "quote": "`INSERT INTO ursitoare.tool_server", "claim": "seedToolServer is a plain INSERT into tool_server with no conflict handling, so a repeated id raises a unique violation."}, {"ref": "src/tools/mcp/register.db.test.ts:137", "quote": "DELETE FROM ursitoare.mcp_server WHERE tenant_id = $1 AND tool_server_id = $2", "claim": "The loop's only cleanup deletes from mcp_server, never from tool_server."}, {"ref": "src/db/migrations/0470_tool_registry.sql:12", "quote": "PRIMARY KEY (tenant_id, tool_server_id));", "claim": "tool_server's primary key is (tenant_id, tool_server_id), so the second seed of srv_bad_check for tenant A violates it."}, {"ref": "src/db/migrations/0470_tool_registry.sql:3", "quote": "tool_server_id text NOT NULL CHECK (tool_server_id ~ '^[a-z][a-z0-9_]{0,31}$')", "claim": "A per-iteration id such as srv_bad_0 satisfies the tool_server_id check, so the alternative fix in option 1 is valid."}]}
