{"ts": "2026-11-23T06:34:44.401815Z", "run_id": "r-20261123T0509Z-33fe", "unit": "openspec:add-mcp-client", "seq": 90, "type": "delegate.result", "question": "Q-004", "id": "Q-004", "status": "answered", "reason": "The test derives the id only from item.endpoint (line 221). Cases 2 (https://mcp.fake.test/mcp) and 5 (http://10.0.0.5:8080/mcp) both have endpoint \"/mcp\", so both give docs__mcp under tenant a. The spec requires registerMcpServerTx to call registerAdapterServerTx, which maps the 23505 unique violation on tool_server to ToolsError TOOLS_EXISTS (store.ts:293), so the fifth good case would reject inside assert.doesNotReject even with a correct implementation. The spec says the good URLs register, so the test, not production code, is wrong; making the id unique per case is the minimal fix and changes no asserted behaviour.", "called": true, "tasks": ["3.1"], "target": null, "kind": "technical", "profile": "delegate-fable", "model": "claude-fable-5-1", "cli": "claude-code", "cost_usd": 0.78185, "decision": "accept", "answer_sha256": "408e8f23bc19ff9bf9a140b706764dbecfef61fee5ffe906bf2b91cd8bd70a3f", "checked": [{"ref": "src/tools/mcp/register.db.test.ts:221", "quote": "const id = `docs_${item.endpoint.replace(/[^a-z0-9]/g, \"_\") || \"root\"}`.toLowerCase().slice(0, 32);", "claim": "The id depends only on the endpoint, so cases with the same endpoint share one id."}, {"ref": "src/tools/mcp/register.db.test.ts:214", "quote": "{ url: \"https://mcp.fake.test/mcp\", local: false, origin: ORIGIN, endpoint: \"/mcp\" },", "claim": "Case 2 has endpoint /mcp."}, {"ref": "src/tools/mcp/register.db.test.ts:217", "quote": "{ url: \"http://10.0.0.5:8080/mcp\", local: true, origin: \"http://10.0.0.5:8080\", endpoint: \"/mcp\" },", "claim": "Case 5 also has endpoint /mcp, so it derives the same id docs__mcp as case 2."}, {"ref": "src/tools/mcp/register.db.test.ts:223", "quote": "await assert.doesNotReject(async () => {", "claim": "Each good case must not reject, so a TOOLS_EXISTS on the fifth case fails the test regardless of the implementation."}, {"ref": "src/tools/store.ts:293", "quote": "throw new ToolsError(\"TOOLS_EXISTS\", \"tool server already exists\", { id });", "claim": "registerAdapterServerTx throws TOOLS_EXISTS when the tool_server id is already taken."}, {"ref": "spec:specs/tool-mcp/spec.md#requirement-registration-stores-the-endpoint-once-and-refuses-what-the-gateway-would", "quote": "else it SHALL call `registerAdapterServerTx` (`mcp`, `surface` null) and insert the endpoint in one transaction", "claim": "The spec requires registerMcpServerTx to go through registerAdapterServerTx, so a duplicate id must throw TOOLS_EXISTS and the good cases need distinct ids."}]}
